translated_text:
Part Three Rights of Victims
Article 15
Women and children victims of acts of violence shall receive the following rights: a. the right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected; b. the right to health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by the victim; c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality, especially regarding their identity; f. the right to compensation;
g. the right to social rehabilitation;
h. the right to complaint handling;
i. the right to assistance; and j. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilitation in the judicial process.

