translated_text:
CHAPTER VII
INVESTIGATION
Article 44
In addition to Investigation Officials of the State Police of the Republic of Indonesia, investigation of criminal acts referred to in (1) this Regional Regulation may be conducted by Civil Servant Officials within the Bengkalis Regency Government whose appointment is determined in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
Civil Servant Investigators as referred to (2) in paragraph (1), are authorized to:
a. conduct examinations on the validity of reports or information concerning criminal acts related to violence against women and children;
b. conduct examinations of any person and/or business entity suspected of participating in criminal acts related to violence against women and children in the business environment;
c. request information from any person and/or business entity in connection with criminal act incidents related to violence against women and children;
d. conduct examinations of evidence, records, or other documents concerning criminal acts related to violence against women and children;
e. conduct examinations at certain places suspected of containing evidence;
f. conduct seizure of goods and materials resulting from violations that can be used as evidence in criminal cases related to violence against women and children;
g. request assistance from experts in the framework of carrying out investigation duties concerning criminal acts related to violence against women and children; and
h. terminate the investigation if there is insufficient evidence of criminal acts related to violence against women and children.
In carrying out their authority, Civil Servant Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1) shall coordinate with the Police in accordance with the provisions (3) of laws and regulations.
(4) Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1) shall notify the commencement of the investigation and submit the results of their investigation to the Public Prosecutor through the Investigation Official of the Police of the Republic of Indonesia in accordance with the provisions stipulated in the Criminal Procedure Law.
